Keep the cpp-rename of got_signal in signal.c (cosmo multicall fold).

signal.c does `#undef got_signal` to neutralise a dead debug macro in
mtools.h, but that also cancels the fold's `#define got_signal
mtools__got_signal`, so signal.o would define the plain symbol while
copyfile/fat/mainloop reference the renamed one. got_signal is
mtools-only, so keeping the rename collides with nothing.

--- a/signal.c
+++ b/signal.c
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 #include "sysincludes.h"
 #include "mtools.h"
 
-#undef got_signal
+/* unpin: keep cpp-rename of got_signal */
 
 int got_signal = 0;
 
